==Old English==

===Etymology 1===
From Germanic ''*deigjōn'' ‘kneader’: cognate with Old Norse [[deigja]] ‘female servant’.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|/ˈdæːje/|lang=ang}}

====Noun====
{{ang-noun|head=dǣġe}}

# female servant
# woman in charge of a [[dairy]]; [[dey]], [[dairymaid]]

